// ============================================================================
//  mod_zapgun.zone  -  the BO1 Zap Guns (dual-wield), v2.9.18
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  User approval 2026-08-31 for queue item 35, after the audit in
//  .agents\WAVEGUN_TARGET_INVENTORY.md: the combined Wave Gun cannot be built
//  (its model exists only in T5 form and nothing on this machine can compile a
//  T6 xmodel), so the split Zap Guns ship as a complete feature in themselves.
//
//  THE DONOR is zone_source\zapgun_donor\mod.ff - a 19-asset minimal fastfile
//  rebuilt from the zm_ezz3.0 package (recipe beside it), --load'ed LAST in
//  build_ff.bat so it can only supply names no zombies fastfile above offers.
//  🛑 A plain --load of their full mod.ff would resolve 77 of this mod's
//  references from a third-party server mod, and their camo_zapgun would drag
//  in the entire camo system including the animated-camo shader this mod runs
//  on - both measured, both are why the donor is minimal (checkpoint 174 §5).
//
//  WHAT IS DECLARED HERE:
//    - the four converted-from-BO1 xmodels and their four materials. Their
//      remaining dependencies (a fiveseven normal-map trio, the
//      zombie_teleporter_glow set, two techsets) resolve from whichever loaded
//      fastfile is first, exactly like every other donor asset - the post-link
//      A/B in checkpoint 174's pre-flight is the check that nothing shared
//      changed owner.
//    - camo,camo_zapgun: NOT the donor's (poisoned - see above). A raw
//      zone_assets\camo\camo_zapgun.json, built in the shape of camo_tesla.json
//      with the zapgun's four base materials, so Pack-a-Punch camos including
//      slot 8 (animated) and slot 12 (Origins blue) work like every other gun.
//      Raw beats every --load for camo (CLAUDE.md precedence table).
//
//  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE:
//    - weapon defs: raw runtime files in weapons\zm\ (all four measured under
//      the 20,480 B loader ceiling), like the Jet Gun and the wpnfix guns.
//    - xanims: 15 raw files in xanim\, packed into mod.iwd - the route the ezz
//      package proved (its mod2.iwd is 818 raw xanims and nothing else).
//    - fx: 6 raw .efx in fx\, like the other wonder weapons' 63.
//    - sounds: alias rows in soundbank\mod.all.aliases.additions.csv with
//      payloads dumped from the donor's own bank.
// ============================================================================
material,mc/mtl_raygun_moon_front
material,mc/mtl_raygun_moon_rear
material,mc/mtl_zapgun_dw1
material,mc/mtl_zapgun_dw2
xmodel,wavegun_le_view
xmodel,wavegun_ri_view
xmodel,wm_zapgun_lh
xmodel,wm_zapgun_rh
camo,camo_zapgun

//  The client half ships as a fastfile script asset like its three siblings
//  (teslagun.csc etc. in mod_wonderweapons.zone); the .gsc needs no line here
//  - Plutonium runs raw scripts/zm/*.gsc straight out of mod.iwd.
script,scripts/zm/zapgun.csc
